WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:02.710
Dispatcher: Faster. Push faster.

00:06.100 --> 00:07.100
Good.

00:07.240 --> 00:08.250
When someone collapses,

00:08.600 --> 00:11.650
a 911 dispatcher talks you through CPR.

00:12.620 --> 00:14.030
Pulse lets you practice that,

00:14.080 --> 00:16.370
hands-on, before you ever need it.

00:17.000 --> 00:18.630
It's for people like Maya,

00:18.680 --> 00:21.930
who learned CPR once,
and have forgotten the rhythm.

00:25.020 --> 00:28.270
Dispatcher: This is CPR practice.

00:28.860 --> 00:32.970
In a real emergency, call 911 first.

00:35.660 --> 00:38.310
911, what's your emergency?

00:40.400 --> 00:42.110
Is he breathing normally?

00:47.700 --> 00:52.250
Kneel beside him.
Hands in the center of the chest.

00:52.920 --> 00:56.890
Push hard and fast. I'll count with you.

01:00.600 --> 01:03.130
Faster. Push faster.

01:06.260 --> 01:08.710
Good. Keep that pace.

01:10.740 --> 01:16.770
Keep going. Don't stop until help
arrives or an AED is available.

01:21.220 --> 01:25.510
You're doing great. Keep going.
Help is on the way.

01:28.540 --> 01:29.990
Your hands are locked together,

01:30.100 --> 01:31.890
and your eyes are on the chest,

01:32.000 --> 01:33.450
so you can't use a phone.

01:34.000 --> 01:37.050
On Specs, the coaching
sits right on your hands.

01:38.140 --> 01:40.590
Pulse was planned with
the Devpost skill pack,

01:40.920 --> 01:43.950
built with CLAD and the Lens Studio MCP,

01:44.360 --> 01:46.970
and every done criterion has a LEAF test.

01:48.780 --> 01:49.760
Pulse.

01:49.760 --> 01:51.950
Practice the rhythm, so
it's there when it counts.
